The first-layer covariance surrogate was worse locally, so I’m dropping it. A more promising low-cost change is at the final layer: use the sampled final preactivation mean/variance with the Gaussian ReLU moment formula instead of averaging sampled ReLUs directly. That should reduce final-layer sampling noise if the last preactivations are close to Gaussian.
